\begin{cases} a^2 + b^2 = 49 \\ \frac{4}{a^2} - \frac{144}{b^2} = 1 \end{cases}
\] We can solve this system by expressing \(b^2\) in terms of \(a^2\) from the first equation and substituting it into the second equation. Solving for \(a\) and \(b\) will give us the ordered pair \((a, b)\). </think> <answer> \((5, 2\sqrt{6})\) </answer>

